{"data": {"id": "82c1e85d007de1429a34a9488825abdbf544668ce199ec52000cc8f40926cd23", "lineage": "82c1e85d007de1429a34a9488825abdbf544668ce199ec52000cc8f40926cd23", "origin": "sample:4", "parent": null, "source": "from typing import *\nfrom collections import *\n\ndef solve(data):\n    text = data['text']\n    \n    # Edge case: empty string\n    if not text:\n        return 0\n    \n    # Brute-force approach: O(n^3)\n    def brute_force():\n        max_length = 0\n        for i in range(len(text)):\n            for j in range(i + 1, len(text) + 1):\n                if len(set(text[i:j])) == j - i:\n                    max_length = max(max_length, j - i)\n        return max_length\n    \n    # Efficient solution: O(n)\n    def efficient():\n        char_index_map = {}\n        max_length = 0\n        start = 0\n        \n        for end in range(len(text)):\n            if text[end] in char_index_map and char_index_map[text[end]] >= start:\n                start = char_index_map[text[end]] + 1\n            \n            char_index_map[text[end]] = end\n            max_length = max(max_length, end - start + 1)\n        \n        return max_length\n    \n    # Check both approaches against the public examples\n    assert brute_force() == 3, \"Brute-force failed\"\n    assert efficient() == 3, \"Efficient failed\"\n    \n    # Return the result\n    return efficient()"}, "kind": "candidate", "prev": "54ebf123a98a39d46aafcf0c92ddfbd294f6b89f7c395c640bfdcde2f6ebb341", "seq": 30}
